Research Engine Phase 3: structured hypotheses, research graph, relevance and the coverage gate

The Research Engine audit's Phase 3 (research intelligence), on top of
Phases 1 and 2. "Which questions measure H1" and "what is affected if I
remove Q6" are one graph query; a generated questionnaire is checked for
being connected to the design. Nothing existing was removed: hypotheses are
still strings by position, every label, tag and plan item still works, and
the verdicts read the same directions (now through one parser).

Schema: HypothesisDetail (type, direction, independent/dependent,
moderator/mediator, group/lower, expected effect, status, note) by index in
research.hypothesisDetails; researchQuestions, kpis and audience on the
research design.

Engine: hypotheses.ts (parseHypothesis, structuredHypotheses, constructFor,
describeHypothesis); set_hypothesis action, add/remove keep the readings
aligned, set_research carries them by statement text and records the new
fields; hypothesis and kpi nodes and edges in the dependency index; impact
reports hypotheses left unmeasured and KPIs that break; relevance.ts
(questionRelevance, removalSet, coverageReport); recognisers for "make the
questionnaire shorter [to N questions | by N | to N minutes]", "remove the
unnecessary questions", "which questions could be removed", "set the
audience to", "make this survey more suitable for X", and H1/hypothesis
labels and KPI names as graph objects; whole-sentence recognisers before the
compound split; coverage links constructs through the resolved sides.

Analytics: hypothesisDirection delegates to the engine's parser; a recorded
direction overrides the words.

Studio: the Research design editor shows each hypothesis's reading and
sections for research questions, KPIs and the audience; the Analysis tab
shows the reading; the outline carries them; the prompt documents
set_hypothesis; "Use in the research design" merges a document card
(mergeDoc.ts); the turn route checks a generation's coverage on the clone and
asks the model once more when it is loose; the card shows the result.

Regression found by the browser corpus and fixed: an applied change's record
joined the AI change history only after the server had numbered it, so the
entry read "Applied …" for a round-trip before "Created …" and undo was not
watching it; commitApplied records it the moment the store takes it and
patches the number in.

Tests: engine 1744 (hypotheses 4, researchGraph 3, relevance 5),
analytics 236, studio 281 (mergeDoc 1), scripts/phase3-research-test.mjs
(8 checks); 13 history-related browser suites and the full corpus green
apart from the 10 known baseline failures. Mutations: engine 36/36 caught,
Studio 11/11 caught. impact.test, copilot.test (prompt cap 14,600) and
phase1-reliability-test adjusted on purpose; see
docs/PHASE3-RESEARCH-2026-10-09.md.

